<title>UK: Alcan to double output at U.K. chemicals plant.</title>
<headline>Alcan to double output at U.K. chemicals plant.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-04-16</dateline>
<text>
<p>Alcan Chemicals Europe, whose ultimate parent is Canada's Alcan Aluminium Ltd is to double output at a speciality chemicals plant in the U.K.</p>
<p>In a release Alcan said it will invest more than 20 million stg into its site in Burntisland, Fife, Scotland over the next two to three years.</p>
<p>&quot;The money will be used to more than double output of a major product line, 'Superfine' alumina trihydrate powders, which are extensively used as flame retardant additives for plastics and rubbers,&quot; it said.</p>
<p>--London Newsroom 44 171 542 8080</p>
</text>
